$DATUM 2-Benzyl-2 methyl-1-(4-nitrophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (4d) To a reaction
vessel charged with RuBr(CO)3(η 3-C3H5) (4.5 mg, 0.015 mmol, 5 mol%),
t-BuPPh2 (10.9 mg, 0.045 mmol, 15 mol%), aldehyde (45.3 mg, 0.30 mmol,
100 mol%) and allene (87.0 mg, 0.60 mmol, 200 mol%) was added toluene
(0.3 mL, 1.0 M) followed by isopropanol (72.1 mg, 1.20 mmol, 400 mol%).
The system was purged with argon gas and the reaction vessel was sealed.
The reaction mixture was allowed to stir at 75 °C for 11 hours, at which
point the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2, 95% toluene:5% EtOAc) to
furnish the title compound (75.0 mg, 0.25 mmol, 83%) as bright yellow oil
(1:1 dr). bright yellow oil.TLC (SiO2): Rf = 0.53, 90% Toluene, 10%
EtOAc. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 8.15 – 8.13 (m, 4H)*, 7.45 – 7.42 (m,
4H)*, 7.26 – 7.19 (m, 6H)*, 7.14 – 7.11 (m, 4H)*, 6.05 (dd, J = 17.6,
10.9 Hz, 1H), 5.84 (dd, J = 17.4, 10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.21 (dd, J = 17.4, 1.0
Hz, 1H), 5.05 (dd, J = 10.9, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 4.85 (dd, J = 17.6, 1.0 Hz,
1H), 4.72 (dd, J = 17.4, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 4.64 (d, J = 4.3 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (d,
J = 2.9 Hz, 1H), 2.92 – 2.64 (m, 4H)*, 2.25 – 2.23 (m, 2H)*, 0.96 (s,
3H), 0.78 (s, 3H). * Signals overlapped 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): 148.8,
148.2, 147.4, 147.2, 141.6, 141.4, 137.4, 137.3, 130.7, 130.6, 128.9,
128.6, 127.8, 127.7, 126.3, 126.2, 122.6, 122.5, 116.7, 115.7, 78.5,
78.4, 46.5 (two signals), 44.2, 43.8, 18.0, 17.5. HRMS Calcd. for
C18H20NO3 (M+1): 298.1443, Found: 298.1447. FTIR(neat): 3154, 2983, 2253,
1519, 1348, 912, 744 cm-1
