$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
11-(tert-Butyl-diphenyl-silanyloxy)-3-hydroxy-4-methyl-undeca-4,9-dienoic
acid allyl ester (51) n-BuLi 1.53 M (770 L, 1.2mmol) was added to
diisopropylamine (165 L, 1.2 mmol) at 0°C. The mixture was stirred at 0°C
for 15 min then diluted with THF (3 mL). The reaction mixture was cooled
to -78°C and was added allyl acetate (127 L, 1.2 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred for 30 min then the aldehyde 50 (400mg, 1.0 mmol) in
THF (3 mL) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 90 min at
-78°C and quenched by addition of saturated aqueous NH4Cl. The mixture
was decanted and the aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc. The combined
organic phases were washed with brine, dried and concentrated under
vacuum. The crude material was purified by flash-chromatography using
EtOAc-hexane (30 : 70). compound 56, yield 77%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cascade Polycyclization: Exploration of a Convergent Route to Access
Various Tricyclic and Tetracyclic Products Related to Sterols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
