$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
(1S,2R)-1-(5-(2-(tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)ethyl)furan-2-yl)-2-methylbut-3-en-1-ol,
14: Freshly sublimed (220 °C, 1 mm Hg) potassium tert-butoxide (7.0 g,
61.38 mmol, 1.2 eq) was dissolved in THF (18 mL), and the mixture was
cooled to -78 °C. Condensed cis-2-butene (23.7 mL, 255.77 mmol, 5.0 eq)
was cannulated into the mixture, then n-butyllithium (1.6 M in hexanes,
38.3 mL, 61.38 mmol, 1.2 eq.) was added dropwise. The resultant solution
was warmed to -50 °C for 20 minutes, then recooled to -78 °C.
(-)-(Ipc)2BOMe (1M in Et2O, 66.5 mL, 66.50 mmol, 1.3 eq.) was added
dropwise and the solution was stirred 30 min. Boron trifluoride etherate
(9.0 mL, 71.61 mmol, 1.4 eq) was added dropwise, followed by dropwise
addition of aldehyde 7 (13.0 g, 51.15 mmol, 1.0 eq.) in THF (10 mL). The
reaction was stirred 3h at -78 °C, then quenched by the addition of 3M
NaOH (13 mL) and 30% hydrogen peroxide (18 mL). The resultant mixture was
stirred at ambient temperature for 12 hours. The layers were separated
and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic
phase was washed with H2O and brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated. The crude residue was purified by FCC (5% EtOAc/Hexanes) to
yield 14 (13.46 g, 76% yield) as a clear oil.
(1S,2R)-1-(5-(2-(tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)ethyl)furan-2-yl)-2-methylbut-3-en-1-ol,
14: 76% yield [α]D -11.2 (c 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.18
(s, 6H), 0.87 (s, 9H), 1.07 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 1.93 (d, J = 5.5 Hz,
1H), 2.66-2.70 (m, 1H), 2.81 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 3.82 (t, J = 7.0 Hz,
2H), 4.49 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 5.04-5.11 (m, 2H), 5.72-5.79 (m, 1H), 5.98
(d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 6.11 (d, J = 3.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
-5.4, 15.1, 18.2, 25.8, 31.9, 42.8, 61.6, 71.4, 106.6, 107.6, 115.7,
139.7, 152.6, 153.5; IR (thin film) 3433 (OH), 2960, 2923, 2854, 1472,
1256, 1109, 999, 905, 836,779 (cm-1); HRMS (ESI) m/z calc’d for
C17H30O3SiNa (M++Na) 333.1856, found 333.1847.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
