$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure using condition set B: A 1 mL
reaction vessel equipped with a stirring bar was charged with acrylamide
(142 mg, 2.0 mmol), DABCO (224 mg, 2.0 mmol) and phenol (188 mg, 2.0
mmol). Note: If the aldehyde component is a solid it is added at this
stage. The vessel was fitted with a septum, gently flushed with Ar gas
and fitted with an Ar balloon. The aldehyde (3.0 mmol) was then added via
syringe. The resulting mixture was heated to 55 °C (whereupon it became
homogeneous) and stirred at this temperature for the time indicated in
Table 3 and then allowed to cool. Column chromatography of the reaction
mixtures (95:5 CH2Cl2/MeOH) yielded the required Baylis-Hillman adducts.
2-[Hydroxy(2-methoxyphenyl)methyl]acrylamide (6), yield 74% M.p. 164-166
°C; IR (film) 3331, 3209, 2938, 1665, 1628, 1600, 1589 cm-1; 1H NMR (400
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 3.75 (s, 3H) 5.30 (s, 1H), 5.38 (s, 1H), 5.75 (s, 1H),
5.78 (s, 1H), 6.93 (m, 3H), 7.21 (m, 2H), 7.45 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 55.4, 65.0, 110.7, 117.9, 120.0, 127.2, 128.3, 130.9, 147.0,
156.3, 169.0; HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C11H13NO3 207.0895, found 207.0891;
Anal. Calcd for C11H13NO3 C, 63.76; H, 6.32; N, 6.76. Found C, 63.51; H,
6.41; N, 6.53.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Baylis-Hillman reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Acrylamide in the Baylis-Hillman Reaction: Expanded reaction scope and
the unexpected superiority of DABCO over more basic tertiary amine
catalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Faltin, Cornelia; Fleming, Eimear M.; Connon, Stephen J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2004), 69(19), 6496-6499

