$DATUM Synthesis of
(1S,2S)-1-{5-[2-(tert-Butyl-dimethyl-silanyloxy)-ethyl]-furan-2-yl}-2-methyl-but-3-en-1-
ol, 8 : Freshly sublimed (220 °C, 1 mm Hg) potassium tert-butoxide (3.9
g, 18.42 mmol, 1.2 eq) was dissolved in THF (5.3 mL) and the mixture was
cooled to -78 °C. Condensed trans-2-butene (14.3 mL, 153.47 mmol, 10.0
eq) at -78 °C was cannulated into the reaction mixture, then
n-butyllithium (1.6 M in hexanes, 11.5 mL, 18.42 mmol, 1.2 eq) was added
dropwise. The resultant solution was warmed to -45 °C for 20 minutes,
then re-cooled to -78 °C. (-)-(Ipc)2BOMe (1M in Et2O, 20 mL, 19.95 mmol,
1.3 eq) was added dropwise, and the solution was stirred 40 min. Boron
trifluoride etherate (2.7 mL, 21.49 mmol, 1.4 eq) was then added
dropwise, followed by aldehyde 7 (3.9 g, 15.35 mmol, 1.0 eq) dropwise.
The reaction was stirred 3h at -78 °C, then quenched by the addition of
3M NaOH (8.7 mL) and 30% hydrogen peroxide (3.9 mL). The resultant
mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 12 hours. The layers were
separated and the aqueous was extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic
phase was washed with H2O and brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The crude residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (5% EtOAc/Hexanes) to yield 8 (3.38 g, 71% yield) as a
clear oil. Synthesis of
(1S,2S)-1-{5-[2-(tert-Butyl-dimethyl-silanyloxy)-ethyl]-furan-2-yl}-2-methyl-but-3-en-1-
ol, 8 yield 71% [α]D -47.70 (c = 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
6.16 (d, 1H, J = 3.2), 6.00 (d, 1H, J = 3.2), 5.77-5.86 (m, 1H),
5.15-5.24 (m, 2H), 4.35 (d, 1H, J = 7.8), 3.84 (t, 2H, J = 6.8), 2.84 (t,
2H, J = 6.8), 2.65-2.74 (m, 1H), 2.1 (bs, 1H), 0.95 (d, 3H, J = 6.8),
0.88 (s, 9H), 0.03 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.22, 152.91,
140.18, 116.81, 108.03, 106.64, 71.38, 61.57, 43.43, 31.94, 25.84, 18.25,
16.39, - 5.43; IR (neat, cm-1) 3434.6, 2929.1, 1558.7, 1471.9, 1103.2,
836.5; HRMS m/z (ESI) calc’d for CC17H30O3SiNa+ (M++Na) 333.1856, found
333.1858
