$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4): To a stirred solution of allyl methyl ether (2.8 mL, 29.9 mmol) in
100 mL of THF at -78 °C was added dropwise s-BuLi (1.0M in cyclohexane,
24 mL, 23.9 mmol). The solution was stirred at the same temperature for
0.5 h then a 1M solution of (+)-Ipc2B(OMe) (7.6 g, 23.9 mmol) in THF was
added dropwise. The reaction was left to stir at this temperature for 1 h
After 1 h, BF3•OEt2 was added dropwise, followed by a solution the of 3 1
(4.0 g, 23.9 mmol) in 20 mL of THF and the reaction was left to stir at
-78 °C for 12 h. The reaction was quenched by the addition of 3.0 M NaOH
(10.4 mL) and H2O2 (30 % in H2O, 4.5 mL, 31.1 mmol). The reaction was
warmed to ambient temperature and stirred for 4 h. The solution was
diluted with Et2O and slowly added to a solution of sat. aq. NH4Cl. The
layers were separated and the aqueous layer was further extracted with
Et2O (3x). The organic layers were combined and washed with sat. aq.
NH4Cl. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated
under vacuum. The crude residue was purified with column chromatography
using 1:1 EtOAc:Hexanes as eluent to afford 5.0 g (88%, Mosher’s ester
analysis revealed >99% ee) of 4, as a yellow oil. Rf = 0.24 (1:1
EtOAc:Hexanes); [α]20 D +15.8 (c = 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
6.95 (1H, s), 6.54 (1H, s), 5.62 (1H, ddd, J = 7.8, 11.0, 16.6), 5.26
(1H, d, J = 16.6), 5.24 (1H, d, J = 10.8), 4.03 (1H, d, J = 7.8), 3.60
(1H, t, J = 7.8), 3.35 (3H, s), 3.05 (1H, bs), 2.70 (3H, s), 2.03 (3H, d,
J = 1.4); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 164.7, 152.9, 137.6, 134.5, 122.6,
120.0, 116.2, 85.4, 80.5, 56.9, 19.5, 14.9; IR (NaCl, neat) 3430, 2980,
2927, 2824, 1645, 1506 cm-1; HRMS (FAB+) Calcd for C12H18NO2S, 240.1058.
Found 240.1062.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, dropwise addition of s-BuLi stage 1, borane stage 2 and
boron trifluoride etherate stage 3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
