$DATUM Pentenol S4. Magnesium metal turnings (5.73 g, 236 mmol) were stirred
vigorously overnight at room temperature in an oven dried round bottom
flask fitted with a condenser under an atmosphere of nitrogen. To the
flask was then added freshly distilled THF (40 mL). A small portion (2
mL) of a 0.9 M solution of 4-bromo-but-1-ene in freshly distilled THF was
added to the suspension of metal, followed by several drops of
1,2-dibromoethane. The reaction mixture was then heated until activated.
Vigorous bubbling was observed. The remaining 0.9 M solution of
4-bromo-but-1-ene in freshly distilled THF (51 mL) was then added to the
reaction mixture dropwise via cannula at 0 ºC. The flask was warmed to
room temperature, and the reaction mixture was heated at reflux for 3 h.
The reaction mixture was subsequently cooled to room temperature and
stirred overnight under an atmosphere of nitrogen. To a solution of
2-(benzyloxy)benzaldehyde (5.00 g, 23.6 mmol) in anhydrous THF (118 mL)
at -78 °C was added 3-butenylmagnesium bromide (7.51 g, 47.1 mmol) via
cannula. The reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C, and the reaction
progress was monitored by TLC. Upon completion, the mixture was warmed to
room temperature, and the reaction was quenched with a saturated aqueous
solution of ammonium chloride. Ether was subsequently added, and the
biphasic mixture was transferred to a separatory funnel. The layers were
separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with ether. The combined
organic layers were washed with brine, dried, filtered, and concentrated
to yield a yellow oil (6.09 g, 96% yield). Pentenol S4, yield (6.09 g,
96% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.46-7.34 (m, 6H), 7.29-7.24 (m,
1H), 7.03-6.96 (m, 2H), 5.91-5.81 (m, 1H), 5.12-4.97 (m, 5H), 2.56 (br s,
1H), 2.29-2.11 (m, 2H), 1.93 (dd, J = 14.4, 7.2 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 155.6, 138.6, 136.8, 132.9, 128.7, 128.3, 128.1, 127.4,
127.1, 121.1, 114.7, 111.8, 70.3, 70.1, 36.6, 30.4; HRMS (EI) calc’d for
C18H20O2: 268.1463; found 268.1459.
