$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the
reaction of (S)-2,3-epoxy-1,1,1-trifluoro-propane ((S)-TFPO, 1) with
electrophiles is followings: An 1.1eq amount of n-BuLi (1.56 M in hexane)
was added dropwise to a solution of (S)-TFPO 1 (1.0 mmol) in THF (5ml) at
-102 °C, and the solution was stirred at the temperature for 10 min to
generate oxiranyl anion 2. Then electrophile (1.5 mmol) was added
dropwise to the solution at the temperature. After the reaction mixture
had been stirred for another 10 min at -102 °C, then ether (1 ml) was
added. The solution was warmed to r.t., followed by addition of sat. aq.
NH4Cl (2 ml). The organic phase was separated, then aqueous layer was
extracted by ether (5 ml ∞ 3). The combined organic layer was washed with
brine (5 ml ∞ 3), dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
(hexane/ethyl acetate 10/1) to give products 3.
4,5-epoxy-1-phenyl-4-trifluoromethyl-1-penten-3-ol (3e): Overall yield
was 77%, ds = 81 / 19, white solid. IR (KBr) 3430 cm-1; mp = 75-77 °C; 1H
NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.28-7.44(m, 5H), 6.80(d, J = 16 Hz 1H), 6.15(dd,
J = 16, 7 Hz 1H), 4.82(dd, J = 7, 3Hz 1H), 3.13(m, 2H), 2.20(d, J = 3Hz
1H) ppm; 19F NMR (188 MHz, CDCl3) δ 89.5(s, CF3, major), 89.1(s, CF3,
minor) ppm; GC/MS m/z (%) 244(13: M+), 133(100), 115(38), 105(30),
77(28), 55(57); Anal Calcd for C12H11F3O2: C, 59.02; H, 4.54. Found: C,
58.62; H, 4.90.
