$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for addition of
2-Lithio-3-methyl-2-butene7 to aldehydes. A solution of s-butyllithium
(2.7 equiv, 1.6 M in cyclohexane) was added dropwise to a -78 °C solution
of 2-bromo-3-methyl-2-butene (3.0 equiv) in THF (1 M). The resulting
solution was stirred at -78 °C for 3 h, then a solution of the
appropriate aldehyde (1.0 equiv) in THF (0.5 M) was added slowly. The
reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 15 min, then quenched with
aqueous NaHCO3 (equal volume to solvent) and allowed to warm to rt. The
resulting mixture was extracted with ether (3 × 25 mL); the combined
organic extracts were dried over sodium sulfate, filtered, and
concentrated. The product was purified by flash chromatography on silica
gel using ethyl acetate/hexanes (1 %→2 %) as the eluant.
(1R,2R)-1-[2-Isopropenyl-2-(triethylsiloxy)cyclohexyl]-3,4-dimethylpent-3-en-2-ol
(23b). Reaction of 0.4 mmol of 19b following the general procedure
afforded109 mg (75 %) of the title compound as a colorless oil. This
material was judged to be a 1:1 mixture of diastereomers by NMR analysis.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.04-5.02 (m, 1 H), 5.00-4.98 (m, 1 H),
4.96-4.94 (m, 1 H), 4.90-4.87 (m, 1 H), 4.67-4.61 (m, 1 H), 4.60-4.55 (m,
1 H), 1.93-1.03 (m, 46 H), 0.99-0.92 (m, 18 H), 0.67-0.61 (m, 12 H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.0, 148.6, 130.6, 129.7, 127.4, 125.7, 112.5,
112.0, 81.5, 81.0, 69.9, 69.7, 39.8, 39.2, 35.5, 35.3, 35.2, 34.6, 28.1,
27.9, 25.4, 23.61, 23.60, 22.6, 22.0, 21.1, 20.2, 20.1, 19.9, 19.6, 12.0,
11.4, 7.4, 7.3, 7.2, 7.0; IR (film) 3385 cm-1. Anal. calcd for
C22H42O2Si: C, 72.07; H, 11.55. Found: C, 71.83; H, 11.59.
