$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(Benzofuran-2-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol (34a). To a flame-dried, round-bottomed
flask, underan argon atmosphere, added benzofuran-2-carbaldehyde (1.24
mL, 10.2 mmol) and ether (20 mL). Placed in an ice bath and added a 1.0 M
THF solution of vinylmagnesium bromide (20.4 mL, 20.4 mmol) dropwise.
Removed ice bath shortly thereafter and let stir at room temperature for
2 hours. Slowly added 50 mL aqueous NH4Cl solution, extracted 3 times
with 20 mL ether, and dried with Na2SO4. Purified via silica gel
chromatography (8:2 pentane:ether). 1-(Benzofuran-2-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol, as
a clear oil, yield 1.52 g, 86%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ 7.55 (2H,
m), 7.48 (2H, m), 7.25 (2H,m), 6.63 (1H, s), 6.19 (1H, m), 5.50 (1H, d, J
= 17.0 Hz), 5.35 (1H, m), 5.34 (1H, d, J = 10.5 Hz). 13C NMR (75.4 MHz,
CDCl3, ppm): δ 157.5, 154.9, 136.3, 127.9, 124.3, 122.8,121.1, 117.2,
111.3, 103.3, 69.1. HRMS (EI) calcd. for C11H10O2: 174.0681,
found:174.0675.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rhenium-Catalyzed 1,3-Isomerization of Allylic Alcohols: Scope and
