$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B2: Synthesis of 2h, 3h, 3i,
and 3t. A solution of 1(672 mg, 4 mmol) in THF (3 mL) was cooled to -78°C
under argon and a solution of n-BuLi (4 mL of a 2M solution in
cyclohexane, 8 mmol) was added dropwise. The reaction mixture was stirred
at -78°C for five minutes and then warmed to -40°C. A solution of the
appropriate benzaldehyde (2.6 mmol) in THF (3 mL) was then added dropwise
and the reaction mixture was allowed to warm to 0°C over one hour. The
reaction mixture was quenched with a saturated solution of NaHCO3 (10 mL)
and ether (10 mL). The phases were separated and the aqueous layer was
extracted with ether (2 × 25 mL). The combined organic extracts were once
washed with 20 ml sat. aq. NaCl, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification of the residue by flash
chromatography (SiO2 ,1% Et3N in eluant). Prepared by General procedure
B2. Purification: SiO2 (20% EtOAc in hexanes containing 1% Et3N) afforded
2h (70%). 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3)7.37 (dd, J=1.6, 8.0 Hz, 1H); 6.92-6.83
(m, 2H); 6.73 (dd, J=1.6, 7.6 Hz, 1H); 5.34 (s, 1H); 4.86 (s, 1H); 4.58
(s, 1H); 1.98 (s, 1H); 1.71 (s, 3H); 0.97 (s, 9H). 13CNMR: (100 MHz,
CDCl3) 144.4; 142.1; 127.8; 127.5; 127.3; 127.0; 115.8; 91.9; 86.3; 61.6;
42.8; 27.0; 25.4. HRMS (ESI): calculated for C16H20NaO2 267.1361 found
267.1198 (M+Na)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM dropwise addition of n-BuLi solution stage 1 and aldehyde stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Intramolecular [2 + 2] Cycloaddition Reactions of Alkynyl Ether Derived
Ketenes. A Convenient Synthesis of Donor-Acceptor Cyclobutanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tran, Vincent; Minehan, Thomas G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(24), 6588-6591

