$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for catalysis experiments
DABCO (5.61 mg, 50.0 μmol) and catalyst 1d (35.6 mg, 50.0 μmol) were
dissolved in 2-cyclohexen-1- one (3) (96.5 μL, 96.1 mg, 1.00 mmol), and
tridecane (15.2 μL, 11.5 mg, 62.5 μmol) was added as internal standard.
The mixture was cooled to 10 °C on a coolable shaker plate and
cyclohexanecarbaldehyde (2) (30.1 μL, 28.0 mg, 250μmol) was added. The
mixture was shaken for 72 h at 10 °C and 400 rpm. Aliquots of 10.0 μL
were taken at intervals and analyzed by GC on chiral stationary phase. In
case of HPLC analysis, the reaction was stopped after 72 h and the
product isolated by column chromatography (n-hexane : ethyl acetate 3 :
1). 2-(Cyclohexyl-hydroxy-methyl)-cyclohex-2-en-1-one (Table 4, entry 1)
2-(Hydroxy-phenyl-methyl)-cyclohex-2-en-1-one (Table 4, entry 2) The
racemic product was prepared following a literature procedure.[2] GC
(Varian CP-Chirasil-Dex, 160 °C (40 min)): τR = 2.16 min (tridecane),
30.13 min ((S)-product, minor), 31.96 min ((R)-product, major). Absolute
configuration was assigned by comparison of the retention times with
those reported by Nagasawa et al.[3]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Morita-Baylis-Hillman Reaction Catalyzed by
Isophoronediamine-Derived Bis(thio)urea Organocatalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Berkessel, Albrecht; Roland, Katrin; Neudoerfl, Joerg M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(19), 4195-4198

