$DATUM General Procedure for the Baylis-Hillman Reaction (Tables 1 and 2). To a
stirred mixture of 2-cyclohexen-1-one (2.0 mmol) and carbonyl compound
(1.0 mmol) in water (1.0 mL) at room temperature was added the amine
catalyst (1.0 mmol). The reaction was stopped by dilution with diethyl
ether and washed with 2 M HCl, followed by water. After drying over
sodium sulfate, filtration, and evaporation, the crude mixture was
analyzed by 1H NMR. 2-(hydroxyphenylmethyl)-2-cyclohexen-1-one, yield 82%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
