$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Carbonic acid
(2E,9E)-(4S,5R,7S,8R)-11-ethoxycarbonyloxy-8-hydroxy-3,5,7,9-tetramethyl-
6-oxo-4-tert-butyldimethylsiloxy-undeca-2,9-dienyl ester ethyl ester
(80). To a -78 °C solution of cHex2BCl (1455 μL, 6.74 mmol) in Et2O (9.7
mL) was added Et3N (1067 μL, 7.76 mmol), followed by a solution of
(-)-(E)-25 (965 mg, 2.57 mmol) in Et2O (19 ml). The reaction was stirred
at -78 °C for 1 h then at 0 °C for 1 h. After cooling to -78 °C, a
solution of 73 (582 mg, 3.40 mmol) in Et2O (4.8 mL) was added. The
mixture was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C and placed in the freezer for 3 d.
Following the same oxidative work-up as for 79, 80 (102 mg, 73%) was
obtained as a colourless liquid after flash chromatography using 30%
Et2O/hexane. Rf = 0.27 (50% hexanes:ether); Carbonic acid
(2E,9E)-(4R,5R,7S,8R)-11-ethoxycarbonyloxy-8-hydroxy-3,5,7,9-tetramethyl-
6-oxo-4- tert-butyldimethylsiloxy-undeca-2,9-dienyl ester ethyl ester
(82). Following the same protocol as for 80 on a 2.71 mmol scale using
(-)-(E)-14, 82 (1.15g, 78%) was obtained as a colourless liquid after
flash chromatography using 50% Et2O/hexane. Rf = 0.27 (50%
hexanes:ether); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.51 (2H, m), 4.66 (2H, d, J =
6.7 Hz), 4.60 (2H, d, J = 7.0 Hz), 4.18 (5H, m), 4.07 (1H, dd, J = 9.3,
4.0 Hz), 2.93 (1H, app dq, J = 7.0, 4.3 Hz), 2.72 (1H, app dq, J = 7.0,
2.1 Hz), 2.54 (1H, d, J = 3.8 Hz), 1.68 (6H, s), 1.29 (6H, m), 1.13 (3H,
d, J = 7.0 Hz), 0.87 (12H, m), 0.05 (3H, s), -0.03 (3H, s); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ 216.8, 155.1, 142.0, 140.8, 122.1, 121.4, 79.3, 78.1, 64.0,
63.8, 51.0, 49.3, 25.8, 18.1, 14.2, 13.9, 13.7, 12.0, 11.1, -4.6, -5.1;
IR (film) ν 3520, 2958, 2932, 1747, 1463, 1370, 1258 cm-1; HRMS (ESI):
m/z calcd. for ([M+NH4]+) = 562.3411, found = 562.3405; [α]20D +43 (c
1.4, CHCl3).
