$DATUM (2E,7E)-3,7-Dimethyl-8-ethoxy-1-(2,6,6-trimethylcyclohex-1-en-1-yl)octa-2,7-dien-5-yn-4-ol
(25).To a solution of enyne 23 (0.6 g, 5.4 mmol) in THF (9 mL) cooled to
-78 °C was added dropwise n-BuLi (9.41 mL, 1.97 M in hexane, 18.5 mmol)
to obtain a clear yellow solution. After stirring for 30 min, a solution
of aldehyde 24 (1.01 g, 4.91 mmol)in THF (9 mL) was added and the
resulting solution was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C and 1additional hour at
25 °C. Saturated aqueous NH4Cl (6 mL) was added and the mixture was
further stirred for 5 min. The two layers were separated and the aqueous
layer was extracted with Et2O (3x). The combined organic layers were
washed with brine (3x), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica
gel (88:10:2 hexane/EtOAc/Et3N) to afford propargylic alcohol 25 as a
thick colorless oil.
(2E,7E)-3,7-Dimethyl-8-ethoxy-1-(2,6,6-trimethylcyclohex-1-en-1-yl)octa-2,7-dien-5-yn-4-ol
(25)., Yield 75% 1H-NMR (250.13 MHz,CDCl3): δ 6.21 (1H, q, J = 1.2 Hz,
H8), 5.43 (1H, t, J = 6.3 Hz, H2), 4.87 (1H, s, H4),3.85 (2H, q, J = 7.0
Hz, O-CH2CH3), 2.72 (2H, d, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H1), 1.88 (2H, t, J = 6.0Hz,
2H3'), 1.80 (3H, s, C3-CH3), 1.65 (3H, d, J = 1.2 Hz, C7-CH3), 1.51 (3H,
s, C2'-CH3), 1.6-1.4 (4H, m, 2H4' + 2H5'), 1.25 (3H, t, J = 7.0 Hz,
O-CH2CH3), 0.95 and0.94 (6H, 2 x s, C6'-2CH3). 13C-NMR (62.89 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 151.0 (d, C8), 136.0(s), 132.9 (s), 128.7 (d, C2), 128.1 (s),
94.2 (s), 92.8 (s), 83.2 (s), 68.6 (t, O-CH2), 68.3(d, C4), 46.0 (t),
39.7 (t), 34.8 (s, C6'), 32.8 (t), 28.2 (q, 2x), 27.0 (t), 19.6 (q), 19.4
(t),17.3 (q), 15.1 (q), 12.1 (q). FT-IR (NaCl): υ 3600-3100 (br, O-H),
2917 (m, C-H),2865 (m, C-H), 2213 (m, C=C), 1645 (s), 1457 (s), 1367 (s),
1308 (s), 995 (m), 859 (m), 743 (m) cm-1. MS m/z (%): 316 (M+, 42), 271
(5), 255 (5), 180 (15), 179 (100),151 (21), 123 (28), 105 (23), 95 (25),
91 (36), 79 (25), 69 (25), 55 (34).
