$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method 2. In a one-necked flask (25 mL) the appropriate aldehyde (10.0
mmol), t-butyl acrylate (10.0 mmol) and DABCO (0.22 g, 2.0 mmol) were
added and the mixture was allowed to react for 15 d at rt. The oil was
then purified by silica gel chromatography (cyclohexane:ethyl acetate
80:20) to give pure adducts 4.Methyl
3-hydroxy-2-methylene-3-(4-nitrophenyl)propanoate (4b), (2.18 g, 87%),
colorless oil. EI MS: m/z (rel intens) 251 (8, M+), 234 (22), 204 (27),
177 (63), 150 (100), 105 (18). Anal. Calcd for C12H13NO5 : C, 57.37; H,
5.22. Found: C, 57.31; H, 5.29.
