$DATUM Methyl 3-hydroxy-3-(4-nitrophenyl)-2-methylenepropanoate (18e).
Purification by column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a
desired compound 18e (187 mg, 79%) as a yellow crystal. Spectral data
were identical to those previously reported.1 TLC: R f 0.33 (2:1
hexane/EtOAc). mp: 70.2 °C (Lit.,1: 73-74 °C). 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
8.21 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.59 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.40 (s, 1H), 5.87
(s, 1H), 5.63 (d, 1H, J = 6.4 Hz), 3.75 (s, 3H), 3.25 (d, 1H, J = 6.4
Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 166.6, 148.8, 147.7, 141.2, 127.5,
127.5, 123.9, 73.0, 52.4. LRMS (FAB) m/z (rel int): 238 ([M+H]+, 5), 260
([M+Na]+, 5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave lower yield
