$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 5i tert-BuLi (1.7 M in pentane, 288 μL, 0.78 mmol, 2.1 equiv)
was added to a solution of the compound 4f (108.0 mg; 0.37 mmol, 1 eq) in
dry THF (3.7 mL) at -78°C. The reaction was allowed to warm to -50°C in
2h; afterwards, it was cooled to -78°C and isovaleraldehyde (48 μL, 0.44
mmol, 1.2 equiv) was added. The temperature was slowly risen to -50°C and
the reaction was stirred at this temperature for 2h. The reaction was
quenched by addition of Et2O and satd aqueous NH4Cl. The aqueous layer
was extracted with Et2O (3x25 mL) and the organic layers were washed with
brine, dried on MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated. The residue was
separated by chromatography (hexane:EtOAc, 95:5) on silica gel to yield
pure 5i (86.3 mg, 78.0%) as a colorless oil. Mixture of diastereomers. IR
(liquid film): 3363; 2955; 2857; 1471; 1361; 1256; 1181; 1084; 989; 898;
835; 774; 669 cm-1. 1H-NMR (300MHz, CD3COCD3) δ: 4.38-4.46 (m, 1H),
4.22-4.31 (m, 1H), 3.55 (d, J = 3.9) and 3.47 (d, J = 4.2 Hz), 1H
overall, (OH); 2.02-2.59 (m, 3H), 1.40-1.79 (m, 3+2 H); 1.05-1.35 (m,
2H); 0.80-0.95 (m, 15H); 0.11, 0.09 (2s, 6H) 13C-NMR (300MHz, CD3COCD3)
δ: 141.7 (s), 141.5 (s), 135.6 (s), 135.5 (s), 82.9 (d), 82.3 (d), 66.8
(d), 66.6 (d), 46.0 (t), 45.7 (t), 34.0 (t), 29.0 (t), 28.3 (t), 26.6
(q), 25.6 (d), 23.9 (q), 23.8 (q), 23.2 (q), 23.1 (q), 19.0 (s),11.9 (q),
11.6 (q), -3.8 (q), -4.2 (q). C17H34OSi (298.54): calcd. C 68.39, H
11.48, O 10.72, Si 9.41; found: C 68.42, H 11.45.
