$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for tandem catalysis
(condition A): A solution of [Pd(allyl)Cl]2 (1.8 mg, 0.005 mmol) and
(S)-i-Pr-PHOX (4.7 mg, 0.0125) in t- AmylOH (1.3 mL) was stirred at room
temperature for 30 minutes. The sequential addition of allylacetate (108
JL, 1.0 mmol), arylaldehyde (1.0 mmol), NHC's salt (0.05 mmol) then DBU
(150 μL, 1 mmol) was followed. After stirring for 20 hours, the solution
was filtrated by suction through a short pad of silica gel with EtOAc
washes. Removal of solvents offer crude material, which was submitted to
chromatography after NMR analysis. 8l, Yield 89%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
