$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Asymmetric Reaction of 1,4-
cyclohexadienyltributyltin (4) (GP1). A 10 mL Schlenk tube was charged
with a stirring bar and flushed with Ar. (S)-BINAP (6.3 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10
mol%), AgOTf (2.6 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10 mol%) and toluene (0.20 mL) were
added. The mixture was stirred under Ar at room temperature for 10
minutes. After cooling to -50 °C, a solution of an aldehyde (0.10 mmol,
100 mol%) in toluene (0.20 mL) was added followed by dropwise addition of
cyclohexadiene 1 (75 mg, 0.20 mmol, 200 mol%). After being stirred for 40
h at -50 °C, the mixture was diluted with pentane. The resulting
suspension was purified by flash chromatography over silica gel to afford
the corresponding homoallylic alcohol (9:1, pentane:MTBE). The
enantiomeric ratio and the absolute configuration were determined after
aromatization using DDQ (GP2).
(S)-Cyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-yl-(4-fluorophenyl)methanol (5a; R = 4-FC6H4)
Homoallylic alcohol 5a (R = 4-FC6H4) was obtained using 4-FC6H4CHO (12
mg, 0.10 mmol) by applying GP1 in 99% yield as a colorless oil. [α]25 D
-87.9 (c 1.00, CHCl3). IR (neat) 3407 (brs), 3029 (s), 2864 (s), 2820
(m), 1604 (s), 1509 (s), 1422 (w), 1223 (s), 1157 (m), 1045 (m), 945 (w),
836 (s), 785 (m), 685 (s) cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.36-7.27 (m,
2H; Ar-H), 7.08-6.98 (m, 2H; Ar-H), 5.97-5.84 (m, 2H; vinyl-H), 5.66-5.46
(m, 2H; vinyl-H), 4.69 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1H; CH-OH), 3.203.09 (m, 1H),
2.702.61 (m, 2H), 1.98 (brs, 1H) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 162.0
(J = 247.4 Hz, s), 137.8 (J = 3.2 Hz, s), 127.83 (d), 127.76 (d), 127.67
(J = 8.0 Hz, d), 125.9 (d), 123.4 (d), 114.9 (J = 21.3 Hz, d), 75.9 (d),
43.4 (d), 26.6 (t) ppm. MS (ESI): 227 ([M + Na]+). HRMS: ([M + Na]+)
calcd for C13H13FONa: 227.0843; found: 227.0836. The enantiomeric ratio
determined by GC analysis was 96 : 4; column, Chiraldex G-TA; temperature
program: 0 min at 100 °C (T0) then a temperature gradient, rate, 0.3 °C
min-1, final temperature 180 °C (TE); tR of R isomer 74.5 min; tR of S
isomer 76.0 min.
