$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Reaction of Thiophenes with n-Butyl Glyoxylate:
(In all procedures with BINOL-Ti catalyst not dried toluene was used and
inert atmosphere is not necessary) Conditions A (for products 9a-9e, 9k):
In a 5 mL round-bottomed flask closed with a septum, 6,6′-Br2BINOL (18.7
mg, 0.042 mmol) was dissolved in 0.8 mL of toluene (not dried). To the
stirred solution of the ligand, titanium tetraisopropoxide (5.9 μL, 5.7
mg, 0.020 mmol, 2.0 mol %) was added via syringe directly under the
solution surface at room temperature (inert atmosphere is not necessary).
The resulting dark red mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature,
diluted with 0.2 mL of toluene, and cooled to -50 °C. n-Butyl glyoxylate
(0.195 g, 1.5 mmol) was introduced and, after 10 min, the corresponding
thiophene (1.0 mmol) was added and stirred for 7 h at -50 °C. The
reaction mixture did not require any work-up and after completion was
directly subjected to flash chromatography using hexane followed by
hexane/AcOEt (9:1) as an eluent. The yields of products obtained from
substituted thiophenes (1a-1e, 1k) were 76-92% (94-98% ee) (see Table 3).
(S)-(5-Methyl-thiophen-2-yl)hydroxyacetic acid butyl ester (9a): oil; 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.87-6.86 (m, 1H), 6.63-6.61 (m, 1H), 5.30 (s,
1H), 4.26-4.17 (m, 2H), 3.39 (s, 1H), 2.46-2.45 (m, 3H), 1.66-1.59 (m,
2H), 1.39-1.28 (m, 2H), 0.91 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CHCl3) δ = 172.7 (C), 140.4 (C), 138.8 (C), 125.4 (CH), 124.9 (CH), 69.1
(CH), 66.2 (CH2), 30.4 (CH2), 18.9 (CH2), 15.3 (CH3), 13.6 (CH3) ppm; IR
(CHCl3) 3474, 2960, 2933, 2874, 1738, 1464, 1382, 1272, 1217, 1201, 1077,
797 cm-1; HPLC analysis: 94% ee (OD-H, 5% i-PrOH in hexane, 1.0 mL/min, λ
= 256 nm, tR = 7.1 min, minor, tR = 12.7 min, major); [α]D 20 = -47.5 (c
= 1.7, CHCl3); HRMS (ESI) calcd. for C11H16O3NaS [(M+Na)+]: 251.07124;
found: 251.06999.
