$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Asymmetric Reaction
of 1,4- cyclohexadienyltributyltin (4) (GP1). A 10 mL Schlenk tube was
charged with a stirring bar and flushed with Ar. (S)-BINAP (6.3 mg, 0.01
mmol, 10 mol%), AgOTf (2.6 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10 mol%) and toluene (0.20 mL)
were added. The mixture was stirred under Ar at room temperature for 10
minutes. After cooling to -50 °C, a solution of an aldehyde (0.10 mmol,
100 mol%) in toluene (0.20 mL) was added followed by dropwise addition of
cyclohexadiene 1 (75 mg, 0.20 mmol, 200 mol%). After being stirred for 40
h at -50 °C, the mixture was diluted with pentane. The resulting
suspension was purified by flash chromatography over silica gel to afford
the corresponding homoallylic alcohol (9:1, pentane:MTBE). The
enantiomeric ratio and the absolute configuration were determined after
aromatization using DDQ (GP2).
(S)-(3-Bromophenyl)(cyclohexa-2,5-dien-1-yl)methanol (5m; R = 3-BrC6H4)
Homoallylic alcohol 5m (R = 3-BrC6H4) was obtained using 3-BrC6H4CHO (19
mg, 0.10 mmol) by applying GP1 in 96% yield as a colorless oil. [α]25 D
-55.4 (c 1.29, CHCl3). IR (neat) 3047 (brs), 3025 (s), 2879 (s), 2817
(m), 1594 (m), 1569 (s), 1474 (m), 1423 (s), 1188 (s), 1095 (m), 1071
(s), 944 (w), 881 (w), 845 (w), 788 (m), 749 (s), 703 (s), 638 (w) cm-1.
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.54-7.51 (m, 1H; Ar-H), 7.42-7.34 (m, 1H;
Ar-H), 7.30-7.18 (m, 2H; Ar-H), 5.99-5.87 (m, 2H; vinyl-H), 5.69-5.43 (m,
2H; vinyl-H), 4.68 (d, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H; CH-OH), 3.22-3.11 (m, 1H),
2.72-2.64 (m, 2H), 2.06 (brs, 1H) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 144.6
(s), 130.3 (d), 129.7 (d), 129.2 (d), 128.2 (d), 128.1 (d), 125.8 (d),
124.7 (d), 122.9 (d), 122.4 (s), 75.6 (d), 43.3 (d), 26.5 (t) ppm. MS
(ESI): 287 ([M + Na]+). HRMS: ([M + Na]+) C13H13 78BrONa and C13H13
80BrONa: 287.0042 and 289.0022; found: 287.0053 and 289.0036.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ag-Catalyzed Stereoselective Cyclohexadienyl Transfer: A Novel Entry into
Arylphenylmethanols
