$DATUM (3S,4S,5E,7Z)-10-(4-Methoxybenzyloxy)-3-ethyl-7-iododeca-1,5,7-
trien-4-ol (15). To a stirred suspension of t-BuOK (11g, 102 mmol) in THF
(100 mL) at -78 °C were added (Z)-2-pentene (17 mL, 153 mmol) and n-BuLi
(2.77 M in hexane, 37 mL, 102 mmol), and the mixture was stirred at -50
°C for 10 min. The mixture was cooled to -78 °C and a solution of
(+)-B-methoxydiisopinocampheylborane (40 g, 128 mmol) in Et2O (80 mL),
BF3·Et2O (32 mL, 255 mmol), and 14 (19 g, 51 mmol) were sequentially
added. After being stirred under dark at -78 °C for 9 h, 3 M NaOH (160
mL) and 30% H2O2 (160 mL) were added, and the mixture was stirred under
dark at 0 °C for 6 h. The reaction mixture was filtered through Celite,
extracted with Et2O, washed H2O and brine, dried, and concentrated.
Purification of the residue by flash column chromatography (SiO2 800 g,
hexane/AcOEt = 30/1-6/1) gave 15 (18 g, 82%) as a pale yellow oil:
(3S,4S,5E,7Z)-10-(4-Methoxybenzyloxy)-3-ethyl-7-iododeca-1,5,7-
trien-4-ol (15). , yield (18 g, 82%) [α]D 25 +26.9 ⁰ ( c 1.00, CHCl3); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.26 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.88 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
2H), 6.01-5.90 (m, 3H), 5.57 (dt, J = 17.0, 9.8 Hz, 1H), 5.19 (dd, J =
10.2, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.14 (dd, J = 17.1, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 4.45 (s, 2H), 4.24
(brs, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.54 (t, J = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 2,59 (dt, J = 6.3, 6.9
Hz, 2H), 2.19-2.14 (m, 1H), 1.58-1.52 (m, 1H), 1.34-1.26 (m, 1H), 0.90
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.1, 137.9, 137.1,
132.6, 130.2, 129.2, 118.4, 113.7, 107.5, 73.6, 72.5, 67.9, 55.2, 52.6,
37.1, 23.1, 11.8; FTIR (film) 3446, 1606, 1512, 1456, 1246, 1092, 1034
cm-1; HRMS (EI) calcd. for C20H27IO3 (M+) 442.1005, found 442.0965.
