$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound S-12 (1.0 g, 5.48 mmol) was dissolved in THF 15 mL, and cooled
to 0 °C. To this solution was added slowly PhMgCl (6.9 ml, 1 M in THF),
and the resulting solution was stirred for 2 min at 0 °C. The solution
was warmed to room temperature before addition of water. The solution was
extracted with ethyl acetate, concentrated under reduced pressure, and
eluted through a silica column (hexane/ethyl acetate: 10/1) to afford
compound S-53 (1.35 g , 5.20 mmol, 95%).
