$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Diol 10: Allene 81 (745 mg, 6.01 mmol) was
added to a suspension of (lIpc)2BH2 (1.72 g, 6.01 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL)
at 0 °C. The suspension was stirred at 0 °C for 1.5 h and then warmed to
room temperature at which time it became homogeneous. This solution was
cooled to -78 °C, and a solution of aldehyde 53 (511 mg, 2.97 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (2 mL) was slowly added down the side of the flask. This solution
was stirred for 5 h at -78 °C, then aldehyde 64 was added dropwise, and
the resulting mixture was allowed to stir at room temperature for ca. 24
h. This reaction mixture was then poured into a suspension of THF (20
mL), water (30 mL) and MeOH (10 mL) containing sodium perborate (3.5 g,
35 mmol) with 10 mL of THF to aid the transfer. After the mixture was
vigorously stirred for 3 h at room temperature, it was diluted with Et2O
and water, and the organic layer was washed with brine and dried (MgSO4).
Concentration of the filtered solution under reduced pressure and
purification of the crude material via column chromatography (SiO2, 4:1
Et2O-hexanes ' 1:1 EtOAc-hexanes) provided 10 as a clear oil (837 mg,
74%, 85% e.e.): Diol 10: [α]D27.0 +11.5 (c 0.20, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) d 7.37-7.27 (m, 5H), 5.74 (dt, J = 15.0, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.56
(dd, J = 15.5, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (s, 2H), 4.08 (app t, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H),
3.88 (bp, J = 5.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.74-3.62 (m, 2H), 2.95 (br s, 1H), 2.90 (d,
J = 5.5 Hz, 1H), 2.25 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 2H), 1.79-1.74 (m, 2H), 1.46 (s,
9H), 1.15 (s, 3H), 1.12 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) d 176.7, 137.9,
131.3, 129.9, 128.4, 127.7, 127.6, 80.9, 77.7, 73.3, 70.4, 68.9, 47.0,
40.4, 35.9, 28.0, 22.5, 20.4; IR (thin film, NaCl) 3436, 3089, 3064,
3031, 2977, 2934, 2872, 1725, 1496, 1470, 1455, 1392 ,1368, 1277, 1255,
1207, 1158, 1117, 1028, 974, 900, 851 , 738 , 698 cm-1; HRMS (ESI)
401.2304 m/z [calc M + Na+ C22H34O5Na 401.2304].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, yield and ee depend on solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective Synthesis of the C(1)-C(11) Fragment of Peloruside A
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Owen, Robert M.; Roush, William R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(18), 3941-3944

