$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Homoallylic Alcohols.
1-(2,4-Dinitrophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (15a). A mixture of
2,4-dinitrobenzaldehyde (9.6 mg, 0.049 mmol), fluorous allytin 6b (92.4
mg, 0.073 mmol), 13a (7.0 mg, 0.0025 mmol), and BTF (2.5 mL) was stirred
at 60 °C for 24 h. After removal of the solvent, the residue was loaded
onto a short column packed with fluorous reverse-phase silica gel (1.0
g). The column was eluted with acetonitrile (3 mL). 15a (11.7 mg, 100%).
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.34-2.44 (m, 2H), 2.70-2.79 (m, 1H), 5.20-5.28
(m, 1H), 5.47 (dd, J = 8.3, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 5.83-5.97 (m, 1H), 8.13 (d, J =
8.7 Hz, 1H), 8.48 (dd, J = 8.7, 2.3 Hz, 1H), 8.82 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H);
EIMS m/z 197 (M - C3H5)+, 149, 103.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM BTF (sic) solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Separation of "Light Fluorous" Reagents and Catalysts by Fluorous
Solid-Phase Extraction: Synthesis and Study of a Family of
Triarylphosphines Bearing Linear and Branched Fluorous Tags
