$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Asymmetric
Baylis-Hillman Reaction. To a solution of chiral ligand 1 (12 mg, 0.03
mmol) in CH3CN (2.6 mL) was added La(OTf)3 (9 mg, 0.015 mmol) at room
temperature under an N2 atmosphere. This was stirred for 10 min, and
benzaldehyde (54 mg, 0.51 mmol), α-naphthyl acrylate (0.10 g, 0.51 mmol),
and DABCO (17 mg, 0.15 mmol) were added sequentially. The resulting
mixture was stirred for 20 min and the reaction quenched with H2O (5 mL).
The mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (10 mL), and the layers were
separated. The organic layer was washed with brine (10 mL), dried
(MgSO4), and concentrated. The crude product was purified by silica gel
using 8/1 hexane/EtOAc as an eluent. The enantiomeric ratios were
determined by HPLC analyses using a chiral column. 0.13 g (88%) of 5E (R1
= Ph) as a white solid HPLC condition: 20/80 2-propanol/hexane (0.6
mL/min). Phenyl (S)-3-Hydroxy-3-phenyl-2-methylenepropanoate. Colorless
oil (75% ee). HPLC condition: 20/80 2-propanol/hexane (0.5 mL/min). 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 200 MHz) δ 7.49-7.21 (m, 8H), 7.05-7.00 (m, 2H), 6.62 (d, J =
1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.11 (d, J = 1.0 Hz, 1H), 5.68 (s, 1H), 3.01 (br, 1H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 50 MHz) δ 164.70, 150.34, 141.89, 141.19, 129.34 (×2), 128.45
(×2), 127.92, 127.21 (×2), 126.72, 125.89, 121.39 (×2), 72.77; MS m/z
(rel intensity) 254 (M+, 5), 161 (100), 133 (45), 117 (95), 94 (95), 77
(45). HRMS m/z 254.0921 (calcd for C16H14O3 254.0943). t R = 15.5 min (R)
and 19.5 min (S).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Baylis-Hillman reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chiral Lewis Acid-Catalyzed Asymmetric Baylis-Hillman Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yang, Kung-Shuo; Lee, Wei-Der; Pan, Jia-Fu; Chen, Kwunmin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2003), 68(3), 915-919

