$DATUM 2-[α-(p-Tolyl)-α-hydroxymethyl]thiophene (7). The condensation of
2-lithiothiophene with p-tolylaldehyde (3.6 g, 3.5 mL, 30.418 mmol)
followed by silica gel column chromatography using petroleum ether/ethyl
acetate (95:5) afforded monool 7 in 79% yield (4.1 g). M. P. 44-47 °C. IR
(KBr film, cm-1) 3381 (OH). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ in ppm) 2.34 (s,
3H), 2.50 (s, 1H), 5.98 (s, 1H), 6.86 (m, 1H), 6.92 (m, 1H), 7.16 (d, J =
7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.23 (m, 1H), 7.27 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 21.3, 72.3, 124.8, 125.3, 126.4, 126.7, 129.3, 137.8, 140.4,
148.5. ES-MS: C12H12SO, calcd av mass, 204.3 obsd m/z 205.2 (M+, 10%),
187.1 (M+-17, 50%). Anal. calcd: C, 70.55; H, 5.92; S, 15.70. Found: C,
70.17; H, 5.74; S, 15.52.
