$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure. To a stirred mixture of
aldehyde (0.5 mmol) and imidazoles (0.5 mmol) in 1M NaHCO3 (2 ml) and THF
(0.5 ml) was added the respective cyclic enones (cyclopentenone,
0.75mmol; cyclohexenone, 1 mmol). The mixture was stirred at ambient
temperature and monitored by TLC. Upon completion or after the indicated
reaction time, the reaction was quenched with 1N HCl and extracted with
ethyl acetate (3ml×3). The organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatograph on silica gel to give the desired
products. 2-[Hydroxy(4-methylphenyl)methyl]-2-cyclopenten-1-one (2E),
yield 87% 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 2.39 (3H, s), 2.44-2.47 (2H, m),
2.58-2.60 (2H, m), 3.49 (1H, br s), 5.53 (1H, s), 7.15-7.18(2H, m),
7.29-7.30 (3H, m); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 20.1, 25.6, 34.2, 68.7,
125.2, 128.1, 136.5, 137.3, 146.8, 158.3, 208.6. HRMS calcd for C13H15O2
(M++1) 203.1066, found 203.1071.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Remarkable Rate Acceleration of Imidazole-Promoted Baylis-Hillman
Reaction Involving Cyclic Enones in Basic Water Solution
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Luo, Sanzhong; Wang, Peng George; Cheng, Jin-Pei
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2004), 69(2), 555-558

