$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure. To a stirred mixture of
sodium methoxide and aldehyde (0.5 mmol) in 2 mL of methanol was added
the respective α,β-unsaturated ketones (0.6 mmol). The resulted mixture
was stirred at room temperature. Upon completion or after the time
indicated in the tables, the reaction was quenched with 1 N HCl and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was extracted with ethyl
acetate. The combined organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography on silca gel to afford the
desired product. 2-[Hydroxy(4-methylphenyl)methyl]-2-cyclopenten-1-one
(14e): yield 77%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 2.39 (3H, s), 2.44-2.47 (2H,
m), 2.58-2.60 (2H, m), 3.49 (1H, br s), 5.53 (1H, s), 7.15-7.18(2H, m),
7.29-7.30 (3H, m); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 20.1, 25.6, 34.2, 68.7,
125.2, 128.1, 136.5, 137.3, 146.8, 158.3, 208.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Baylis-Hillman Reactions of Cyclic Enones in Methanol As
Catalyzed by Methoxide Anion
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Luo, Sanzhong; Mi, Xueling; Xu, Hui; Wang, Peng George; Cheng, Jin-Pei
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2004), 69(24), 8413-8422

