$DATUM tert-butyl
(4R,8S,E)-4-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-8-hydroxyundeca-6,10-dienylcarbamate
(5) A pressure tube was charged with [Ir(cod)Cl]2 (0.064 g, 0.095 mmol,
2.5 mol%), (S)-Cl,OMe-BIPHEP (0.124 g, 0.190 mmol, 5 mol%),
4-chloro-3-nitrobenzoic acid (0.077 g, 0.380 mmol, 10 mol%) and cesium
carbonate (0.247 g, 0.760 mmol, 20 mol%) and then carefully purged with
argon. Dry tetrahydrofuran (5 mL) was added followed by allyl acetate
(0.42 mL, 3.86 mmol, 200 mol%). Pressure tube was sealed and reaction was
stirred at room temperature for 5 minutes. Then reaction was heated to
80°C for one hour. Reaction was allowed to cool to room temperature. Enal
4 (1.41 g, 3.80 mmol, 100 mol%) was dissolved in dry tetrahydrofuran (7
mL) and cannulated into reaction mixture followed by addition of
iso-propanol (1.45 mL, 19.0 mmol, 500 mol%). Pressure tube was sealed
avoiding air contamination and the heated to 80°C for 24 hours. Reaction
mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature. Mixture was diluted with
dichloromethane (12 mL) and solids were filtered off trough celite pad
followed by dichloromethane washings. Solvents were evaporated to dryness
to give 2.30 g of brown oil. Crude product was purified by silica gel
chromatography using 15-20% ethyl acetate in hexanes to afford 1.31 g
(83%) of alcohol 5 as clear oil. tert-butyl
(4R,8S,E)-4-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-8-hydroxyundeca-6,10-dienylcarbamate
(5), yield 1.31 g, 83% TLC (SiO2): Rf = 0.40 (25% ethyl acetate in
hexanes). [α]23 D = +6 (c = 1.0, CH2Cl2). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
5.72-5.86 (m, 1H), 5.63 (dt, J = 15.3, 7.1 Hz, 1H), 5.50 (dd, J = 15.4,
6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.05-5.16 (m, 2H), 4.58 (br s, 1H), 4.05-4.16 (m, 1H),
3.60-3.75 (m, 1H), 2.96-3.18 (m, 2H), 2.11-2.38 (m, 4H), 1.84 (br s, 1H),
1.34-1.61 (obs m, 4H), 1.42 (obs s, 9H), 0.86 (s, 9H), 0.03 (s, 3H), 0.02
(s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 156.1, 134.7, 134.5, 128.1, 118.1,
79.2, 71.9, 71.7, 42.1, 40.8, 40.3, 33.8, 28.5, 26.0, 25.9, 18.2, -4.3,
-4.4. FTIR (film): υ 3351, 2952, 2929, 2856, 1690, 1513, 1472, 1462,
1390, 1365, 1250, 1170, 1087, 1039, 1004, 972, 937, 912, 834, 809, 773,
732 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) Calcd. for C22H43NO4SiNa [M+Na]+: 436.2859, found:
436.2856. HPLC: Diastereomeric purity was determined by HPLC analysis of
O-benzoate derivative of the product. (Chiralcel OD-H + OD-H column, 0.3%
i-PrOH in hexanes, 1.0 mL/min, 230 nm), tminor = 58.0 min and 59.5 min,
tmajor = 68.8 min and 73.2 min; ee 92%, dr 30:1.
