$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the synthesis of
1,3-disubstituted propargyl alcohols (4a-4o). nBuLi (1.6M solution in
hexane, 1.5 mmol, 1.06 ml/mmol alkyne) was added to a degassed solution
of terminal alkyne (1equiv) in dry THF (5ml/mmol alkyne) at -78 °C under
nitrogen atmosphere. The mixture was stirred for 1h at -78 °C before
aldehyde (1 equiv in 4ml THF) was added. The reaction mixture was warmed
to room temperature and stirred for 1h, and after completion of the
reaction as analyzed by TLC, the solvent was removed in vacuo. The
reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc (5 ml) and quenched with a
saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution. The aqueous mixture was extracted with
EtOAc (10 ml x 3), and the combined organic layers were washed with brine
(10 mL). After the organic layer was dried with anhyd. Na2SO4, the
solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by
silica gel chromatography or by crystallization with hexane and EtOAc to
give propargylic alcohols 4a to 4o. Compound 4i, yield 71%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tandem C-2 Functionalization-Intramolecular Azide-Alkyne 1,3-Dipolar
Cycloaddition Reaction: A Convenient Route to Highly Diversified
9H-Benzo[b]pyrrolo[1,2-g][1,2,3]triazolo[1,5-d][1,4|diazepines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
