$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-((Z)-2-Phenylethynyl-1-cyclooctenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (6a); Following the
General Procedure E; General Procedure E. To a stirred solution of 11
(4.50 mmol) in Et2O (25 ml) was added allyl Grignard reagent (0.81 M
solution in Et2O, 9.00 mmol) at 0 °C and stirred for 30 min. The mixture
was then quenched by addition of saturated aq. NH4Cl, extracted with
EtOAc three times, and washed with brine. The organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography to give 6.
1,3,5-tris(2-((Z)-(1-hydroxy-3-butenyl)-1-cyclooctenyl)ethynyl)benzene
(6r); Following the General Procedure E, Grignard reagent (6 equiv) was
used; the reaction was carried out in THF/E2O (3/1); purified by silica
gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 3/1) (Diastereomeric mixture:
76% yield, pale yellow solid); The following data are for a mixture of
four diastereomers (the diastereomer ratio was not assigned). 1H NMR
(CDCl3 ) δ 1.47-1.52 (m, 12.0H), 1.61-1.73 (m, 12.0H), 1.80 (m, 3.0H),
2.29-2.48 (m, 18.0H), 5.00-5.05 (m, 3.0H), 5.13-5.17 (m, 3.0H), 5.16-5.21
(m, 3.0H), 5.85-5.93 (m, 3.0H), 7.35 (s, 3.0H); 13C NMR (CDCl3 ) δ 25.98,
26.13, 26.64, 28.43, 31.14, 31.46, 40.50, 73.68, 90.21, 91.93, 117.85,
118.98, 124.31, 133.00, 134.94, 150.23; HRMS (FAB) calcd for C48H60O3
(M+) 684.4542, found 684.4528.
