$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B for the Four-Component
Sequence Anhydrous zinc iodide (20 mol %), zinc powder (20 mol %), iron
powder (20 mol %) and CoBr2(py-imine) (10 mol %) (py-imine =
2,4,6-trimethylphenyl-N-(pyridin-2-ylmethylene)-aniline) were suspended
in 0.5 mL anhydrous dichloromethane under argon atmosphere. Then
boroprene 1 (1.0 equiv) and the enyne 3 (1.0 equiv) were added and the
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 16 h. Afterwards the
suspension was treated with the diene 5 (1.2 equiv) and additional
anhydrous zinc iodide (20 mol %), zinc powder (20 mol %) and
CoBr2(ligand) (10 mol %) and stirred for 16 h at room temperature. Then
the reaction mixture was diluted with 0.5 mL of anhydrous dichloromethane
and cooled to 0°C. After addition of the aldehyde (1.0 equiv) the mixture
was stirred for 1 h. The suspension was then brought to room temperature
and was quenched via injection of triethanolamine (1.1 equiv). After
stirring for 1 h at room temperature the reaction mixture was filtered
over a short pad of silica gel (pentane/diethyl ether 1:1) and the
solvent was removed under vacuum. The residue was then purified by flash
column chromatography.
rac-(R)-1-((S)-3-(4,5-Dimethyl-2-methylenehex-4-enyl)-6-methylene-4-phenylcyclohex-3-enyl)-2-methylpropan-1-ol
(7a) According to the general procedure B the catalyst was prepared from
zinc iodide (32 mg, 0.10 mmol), zinc powder (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and
CoBr2(py-imine) (22 mg, 0.05 mmol) in 0.5 mL dichloromethane. Then
boroprene 1 (97 mg, 0.50 mmol) and pent-4-en-1-ynylbenzene (71 mg, 0.50
mmol) were added to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred
for 16 h. Then the suspension was treated with 2,3-dimethyl-1,3-butadiene
(70 μL, 0.60 mmol), additional anhydrous zinc iodide (32 mg, 0.10 mmol),
zinc powder (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe) (31 mg, 0.05 mmol) and was
stirred for 16 h at room temperature. After dilution and cooling to 0°C
isobutyraldehyde (50 μL, 0.50 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture
was stirred at this temperature for 1 h. After quenching with
triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55 mmol), work up and purification by flash
column chromatography (silica gel, pentane/diethyl ether 10:1),
rac-(S,E)-1-((S)-3-(4,5-Dimethyl-2-methylenehex-4-enyl)-6-methylene-4-phenylcyclohex-3-enyl)-2-methyl-3-phenylprop-2-en-1-ol
(7c) According to the general procedure B the catalyst was prepared from
zinc iodide (32 mg, 0.10 mmol), zinc powder (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and
CoBr2(py-imine) (22 mg, 0.05 mmol) in 0.5 mL dichloromethane. Then
boroprene 1 (97 mg, 0.50 mmol) and pent-4-en-1-ynylbenzene (71 mg, 0.50
mmol) were added to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred
for 16 h. Then the suspension was treated with 2,3-dimethyl-1,3-butadiene
(70 μL, 0.60 mmol), additional anhydrous zinc iodide (32 mg, 0.10 mmol),
zinc powder (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe) (31 mg, 0.05 mmol) and was
stirred for 16 h at room temperature. After dilution and cooling to 0°C
(E)-2-methyl-3-phenylacrylaldehyde (70 μL, 0.50 mmol) was added and the
reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature for 1 h. After quenching
with triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55 mmol), work up and purification by
flash column chromatography (silica gel, pentane/diethyl ether 5:1), The
desired product 7c was obtained as an orange oil (159 mg, 0.36 mmol,
73%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 7.38-7.20 (m, 10H), 6.52 (s, 1H), 5.08
(s, 2H), 4.75 (s, 1H), 4.71 (s, 1H), 4.33 (d, J = 10.0 Hz, 1H), 3.32-3.06
(m, 2H), 2.72-2.42 (m, 5H), 2.34 (dt, J = 17.3, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 2.21-1.99
(m, 2H), 1.92 (s, 3H), 1.58 (s, 3H), 1.50 (s, 3H), 1.45 (s, 3H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ = 145.7, 145.6, 142.5, 137.8, 137.4, 133.3, 129.5,
129.2, 129.0, 128.1, 127.8, 126.6, 126.1, 124.9, 111.0, 110.4, 77.8,
45.6, 41.5, 40.8, 38.3, 33.1, 20.5, 20.3, 18.3, 12.2. IR (film, cm-1):
3419, 3066, 3021, 2981, 2911, 2358, 1645, 1599, 1489, 1437, 1369, 1249,
1174, 1009, 890, 750, 697, 555, 508. HRMS (EI): calculated for C32H38O:
m/z = 438.2923; found m/z = 438.2916.
