$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of ethyl propriolate (300 mg, 3.05 mmol) in dry THF (2 mL)
was added a LDA solution [prepared from n-BuLi (1.0 mL, 2.5 M in hexane)
and i-Pr2NH (0.36 mL) in THF(15 mL)] at - 78 °C under nitrogen. After
stirring at -78 °C for 1 h, the mixture was warmed up to 0 °C, and
compound 17 (400 mg, 2 mmol) in THF (3 mL) was added, and reaction
mixture was then stirred at room temperature for 30 min. The reaction was
quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl (10 mL), and the mixture was
then extracted with Et2O (3 x 30 mL). The combined extracts were first
washed with brine (2 x 10 mL), and then dried over Na2SO4. The solvent
was removed under vacuum, and the residue was purified by a flash
chromatography on silica gel (PE/ethyl acetate = 8/1) to give the adduct
(590 mg) in 98% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthetic Study of 1,3-Butadiene-Based IMDA Approach to Construct a
[5-7-6] Tricyclic Core and Its Application to the Total Synthesis of
C8-epi-Guanacastepene O
