$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of ethyl propriolate (100 mg, 1.0 mmol) in dry THF (2 mL)
was added dropwise by syringe to a pre-prepared solution of LDA [n-BuLi
(330 μL, 2.5 M in hexane) and i-Pr2NH (120 μL) in THF (4 mL)] at -78 °C
under nitrogen, and the mixture was stirred at the same temperature for 1
h. To this solution was added compound 22 (80 mg, 0.40 mmol) in THF (2
mL) at -78 °C, and the formed solution was stirred at the same
temperature for an additional hour. The reaction was quenched by addition
of a saturated solution of NH4Cl (2 mL), and then extracted with Et2O (3
x 10 mL). The combined extracts were washed with brine (2 x 5 mL), and
dried over Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under vacuum and the residue
was purified by a flash chromatography (silica gel, petroleum/ethyl
acetate = 8/1) to give the adduct (115 mg) in 95% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthetic Study of 1,3-Butadiene-Based IMDA Approach to Construct a
