$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2. General procedure for the synthesis homoallyl alchoals: A mixture of
1-bromo-2-propene (3 mmol) or 1-bromo-2-methyl-2-propene (3 mmol), indium
metal (1.2 mmol) and sodium iodide (3 mmol) in dimethylformamide (3-4 mL)
was stirred at rt until the complex was completely formed. A solution of
bromoaldehyde in dimethylformamide was then added to the reaction
mixture. The reaction was monitered by TLC change and after 5-6h the
reaction mixture was quenched with a few drops of 1N HCl solution. It was
then extracted with dichloromethane which was thoroughly washed with
sodium thiosulphate and then brine water. Evaporation of the solvent
followed by purification by silica gel (60-120 mesh) column
chromatography provided the pure product. Compound (2a) , yellow liquid,
yield 82%, 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400MHz) δ: 1.90 (d,1H, J= 2.8 Hz), 2.34-2.45
(m, 3H), 2.53-2.63 (m,1H), 2.76-2.85 (m, 2H), 5.08 (m,1H), 5.10- 5.21 (m,
2H), 5.81-5.92 (m, 1H), 7.11(d, 1H, J= 7.2Hz), 7.14-7.24 (m, 2H), 7.63
(d,1H, J= 7.6) 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100MHz) δ: 24.26, 27.92, 39.24, 73.38,
118.28, 118.51, 126.65, 126.87, 127.08, 127.96, 133.74, 133.85, 136.56,
141.03.
