$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM b) Methylmagnesium bromide addition: Methylmagnesium bromide (1M in THF,
1.1 equiv) was added dropwise to a solution of the corresponding aldehyde
Ib-f in THF (0.1M) at 0ºC. The mixture was stirred, while the reaction
temperature was allowed to rise. The progress of the reaction was
monitored by means of TLC. When the starting material was consumed
(approximately one hour), the mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl and extracted with ethyl acetate several times. The combined
organic layers were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated under
vacuum. Crude product II, which was purified in each case as described
below. (E)-Ethyl 3-(2-(1-hydroxyethyl)-4-methoxyphenyl)acrylate (IIb):
Flash chromatography of the crude reaction product [n-hexane:EtOAc
(5:1)]. A yellow oil (90%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.31 (t, J=7.1,
3H), 1.48 (d, J=6.5, 3H), 3.85 (s, 3H), 4.26 (q, J=7.1, 2H), 5.33 (q,
J=6.4, 1H), 6.26 (d, J=15.8, 1H), 6.82 (dd, J1=8.6 J2=2.7, 1H), 7.16 (d,
J=2.7, 1H), 7.52 (d, J=8.7, 1H), 7.97 (d, J=15.9, 1H). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 14.3 (CH3), 25.1 (CH3), 55.4 (CH3), 60.4 (CH2), 66.5 (CH), 110.3
(CH), 113.5 (CH), 117.9 (CH), 124.0 (C), 128.3 (CH), 140.6 (CH), 146.9
(C), 161.5 (C), 167.2 (C). HRMS (EI) calcd for C14H18O4 [M++Na]:
273.1097, found: 273.1093.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction, dropwise addition of MeMgBr (stage 1)
