$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure for the Syntheses of βaylis-Hillman Adducts
using the DMAP, DMAP·HCl protocol. Preparation of ethylthio
2-hydroxycyclopent-1(5)-enyl ketone (4). To a stirring solution of
aldehyde 3 (30.0 mg, 0.174 mmol) in 1.74 mL of EtOH (absolute) in a 4 mL
vial was added 4-(dimethylamino)pyridine (21.3 mg, 0.174 mmol) and
4-(dimethylamino)pyridine hydrochloride (7.0 mg, 0.044 mmol). The
reaction mixture was heated at 78 °C for 1 h, after which time TLC
analysis indicated complete consumption of starting material. The mixure
was diluted with 100 mL of CH2Cl2 , washed with H2O (2 × 10 mL), brine (2
× 15 mL), dried over NaSO4 , filtered, and then concentrated under
reduced pressure. Purification was accomplished by flash chromatography
on a 1.5 × 23 cm column eluting with 20% EtOAc/hexanes, collecting 4 mL
fractions. The product containing fractions (36-45) were combined and
concentrated under reduced pressure to give Baylis-Hillman adduct (4)
(26.0 mg, 87% yield) as a colorless oil. ethylthio
2-hydroxycyclopent-1(5)-enyl ketone (4). Rf 0.48 (50% EtOAc/hexanes); 300
MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.93 (t, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 5.22-5.10 (m, 1H),
3.05-2.88 (m, 2H), 2.80 (br d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 2.76-2.59 (m, 1H),
2.52-2.27 (m, 2H), 1.96-1.80 (m, 1H), 1.30 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H); 75 MHz
13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 190.4, 145.3, 144.9, 76.0, 32.0, 31.3, 23.1, 15.0; IR
(neat) 3424 (br), 2966, 2929, 1656, 1615, 1266, 1163, 1056 cm-1; Anal.
Calcd for C8H14O2S: C, 55.78; H, 7.02; S, 18.62. Found C, 55.49; H, 6.89;
S, 18.40.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study - solvents and temp.
