$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure for the Syntheses of Baylis-Hillman Adducts
using PMe3. Preparation of ethylthio 2-hydroxycyclopent-1(5)-enyl ketone
(4). To a stirring solution of aldehyde 3 (34.0 mg, 0.197 mmol) in 10 mL
of CH2Cl2 in a 15 mL round bottom flask was added trimethylphosphine (2.0
μL, 0.02 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at rt for 15 h after
which time TLC analysis indicated complete consumption of starting
material. The mixture was concentrated under reduced pressure.
Purification was accomplished by flash chromatography on a 1.75 × 20 cm
column eluting with 5% EtOAc/hexanes collecting 4 mL fraction. The
product containing fractions were combined and concentrated under reduced
pressure to give Baylis-Hillman adduct (4) (28.0 mg, 82% yield) as a
colorless oil. Analytical Data for ethylthio 2-hydroxycyclopent-1(5)-enyl
ketone (4). Rf 0.48 (50% EtOAc/hexanes); 300 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.93
(t, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 5.22-5.10 (m, 1H), 3.05-2.88 (m, 2H), 2.80 (br d, J
= 2.0 Hz, 1H), 2.76-2.59 (m, 1H), 2.52-2.27 (m, 2H), 1.96-1.80 (m, 1H),
1.30 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H); 75 MHz 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 190.4, 145.3, 144.9,
76.0, 32.0, 31.3, 23.1, 15.0; IR (neat) 3424 (br), 2966, 2929, 1656,
1615, 1266, 1163, 1056 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C8H14O2S: C, 55.78; H, 7.02;
S, 18.62. Found C, 55.49; H, 6.89; S, 18.40.
