$DATUM 2-[Hydroxy(2-methoxyphenyl)methyl]acrylic Acid Ethyl Ester. Ethyl
acrylate (120 mg, 1.2 mmol), o-anisaldehyde (136 mg, 1.0 mmol), formamide
(225 mg, 5.0 mmol), ytterbium triflate (31 mg, 0.05 mmol), and
3-hydroxyquinuclidine (127 mg, 1.0 mmol) were reacted. Purification by
column chromatography using 10% ethyl acetate in hexane as eluant gave
the adduct as a pale yellow oil (212 mg, 90%):
2-[Hydroxy(2-methoxyphenyl)methyl]acrylic Acid Ethyl Ester, yield 212 mg,
90%
