$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 1-Formyl-6-benzoyl-1,5-dien-3-yne Compound 12 (Scheme S1).
To a solution of 1-formyl-ene-yne compound 3S1 (2.1 g, 10 mmol) in THF
(10 mL) was added phenylmagnesium bromide (11 mL, 11 mmol, 1.0 M in THF)
at 0 °C and the mixture was stirred for at room temperature for 1 h. The
reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution and the
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (10 mL×3). The combined organic
layer was washed with water and dried over MgSO4. The organic solvent was
removed under reduced pressure and the residue in DMSO (1.0 mL) was added
KF (21 mg, 697 mg, 12 mmol) at room temperature. After stirring for 30
min, the reaction was quenched with water at 0 °C and the aqueous layer
was extracted with Et2O (10 mL×3). The combined organic layer was washed
with water and dried over MgSO4. The organic solvent was removed under
reduced pressure and the residue was subjected to flash column
chromatography on silica gel with hexane/AcOEt (v/v = 10/1) as eluents to
afford alcohol 20 Yellow solid, (2.0 g, 9.3 mmol, 93%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 1.49-1.65 (m, 4H), 2.21-2.25 (m, 4H), 3.16 (s, 1H), 6.11 (s,
1H), 7.22-7.26 (m, 1H), 7.30-7.32 (m, 2H), 7.43 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd- and Cu-Catalyzed One-Pot Multicomponent Synthesis of Hetero
α,α'-Dimers of Heterocycles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
