$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for mono-lithiation:
1,1-Dibromo-3,3,3-trifluoro-2-((methoxymethoxy)methyl)prop-1-ene (164 mg,
0.5 mmol) dissolved in THF (5 mL) and the mixture was cooled to -78°C.
Butyl lithium (2 mol/L in cyclohexane, 0.25 mL, 0.5 mmol) was added
slowly to the mixture. The reaction was quenched with methanol after
stirred for 0.5 h at -78°C. The ratio of isomer was determined by 19F NMR
of the quenched mixture. The mixture was diluted with ether (50 mL),
washed with water (3×50 mL) and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Removing the
solvent and subsequent column chromatography give
1-bromo-3,3,3-trifluoro-2-[(methoxymethoxy)methyl]prop-1-ene as a
colorless oil.
(E)-2-bromo-4,4,4-trifluoro-3-[(methoxymethoxy)methyl]-1-phenylbut-2-en-1-ol,
pale yellow oil, yield 93%; νmax (neat) /cm-1 3420, 2953, 2893, 1631,
1452, 1309, 1174, 1129, 1033, 700; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.43-7.37
(m, 5H), 7.00 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 4.70 (s, 2H), 4.51 (s, 2H), 3.42 (s,
3H), 3.00 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H); 19F NMR (282 MHz) δ -55.86; 13C NMR (75.5
MHz) δ 147.28 (q, J = 3.5 Hz), 139.07, 128.85 (q, J = 29.7 Hz), 128.26,
128.12, 125.82, 122.83 (q, J = 277.6 Hz), 96.23, 71.95 (q, J = 2.9 Hz),
66.59 (q, J = 2.0 Hz), 55.60; MS (EI) m/z 292 (M+. -62, 6.2), 45 (100);
Anal Calcd for C13H14BrF3O3: C, 43.97; H, 3.97; Found: C, 44.35; H, 4.20.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
