$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for all Diorganozinc
Additions Except Entry 11; Compounds 12a and 12s. Vinyl Adduct 5a. To
1.47 mL of a 1.0 M solution of vinylmagnesium bromide in THF was added
0.61 mL of THF. The solution was cooled to -30 °C, and 1.47 mL of a 0.5 M
solution of dry zinc chloride in ether was added dropwise. The white
suspension was stirred for 30 min. To the newly formed divinylzinc
reagent was added a solution of 2a (0.108 g, 0.367 mmol) in 0.61 mL of
THF at -30 °C. The reaction was stirred at -25 °C for 18 h and was then
quenched at -30 °C with 3 mL of saturated NH4Cl. After warming to room
temperature, the reaction mixture was diluted with ether and washed three
times with water, and the water layer was back-extracted once. The
organics were dried with anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and then
concentrated in vacuo. 2-Methyl-1-propenyl Adduct 14a: Light yellow oil
(79% yield); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 5.97 (m, 1H), 5.68 (m, 1H), 5.31
(d, J = 9.44 Hz, 1H), 4.17 (d, J = 9.48 Hz, 1H), 2.81 (s, 1H), 2.35 (m,
6H), 2.15 (m, 2H), 1.73 (s, 3H), 1.67 (s, 3H), 1.21 (m, 2H), 0.78 (s,
3H); 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 134.6, 131.7, 127.2, 121.7, 75.7, 64.6,
40.4, 30.8, 27.8, 26.2, 22.3, 20.4, 18.6; IR (neat film) 3630-3100, 2965,
2832, 1675, 1450, 1374, 1037, 1021, 842 cm-1; HRMS-CI (m/z) [M+H] calcd
for C14H26NO 224.201739, found 224.201235.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Remarkable diastereoselectivity in the addition of allylic and
unsaturated diorganozinc reagents to β-(N,N-dialkylamino) aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Soucy, Regina L.; Kozhinov, Denis; Behar, Victor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2002), 67(6), 1947-1952

