$DATUM (E)-7-Phenyl-4-(toluene-4-sulfonyl)-7-triethylsiloxyhept-4-en-3-ol 2b To
a solution of 310 mg (740 μmol, 1.0 equiv) of vinyl sulfone 1'b in 9 mL
of THF at -78°C was added dropwise 1.4 mL (820 μmol, 1.1 equiv) of a 0.58
M solution of PhLi.LiBr in ether. The resulting solution was stirred at
-78°C for 15 min and 64 μL (890 μmol, 1.2 equiv) of freshly distilled
propionaldehyde was then added. The reaction mixture was stirred at -78°C
for 20 min, quenched with 5 mL of a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution and
diluted with 100 mL of ethyl acetate. The layers were separated and the
organic layer was washed with brine, dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (ether/petroleum ether 10:90, 15:85, 20:80,
25:75, 30:70) to afford 229 mg (65%) of a 1:1 mixture of the 2
diastereomers of 2b as a colorless oil and 53 mg of starting vinyl
sulfone 1'b (corrected yield: 78%)
(E)-7-Phenyl-4-(toluene-4-sulfonyl)-7-triethylsiloxyhept-4-en-3-ol 2b,
yield 1H NMR(400MHz, CDCl3): I 7.71-7.68 (m, 1H), 7.67-7.65 (m, 1H),
7.31-7.22 (m, 7H), 7.00 (dd, J = 9.3, 7.0 Hz, 0.5H), 6.90 (dd, J = 8.1,
7.1 Hz, 0.5H), 4.87 (dd, J = 6.3, 5.4 Hz, 0.5H), 4.81 (dd, J = 7.9, 4.3
Hz, 0.5H), 4.39 (dt, J = 8.7, 5.0 Hz, 0.5H), 4.34 (ddd, J = 11.4, 6.1,
5.5 Hz, 0.5H), 3.02 (ddd, J = 14.3, 9.3, 7.9 Hz, 0.5H), 2.91 (d, J = 5.0
Hz, 0.5H), 2.85 (ddd, J = 14.7, 8.1, 5.4 Hz, 0.5H), 2.71 (ddd, J = 14.7,
7.1, 6.3 Hz, 0.5H), 2.56 (ddd, J = 14.2, 7.0, 4.3 Hz, 0.5H), 2.43 (s,
3H), S5 2.37 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 0.5H), 1.73-1.59 (m, 1H), 1.54-1.40 (m, 1H),
0.86 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 4.5H), 0.83 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 4.5H), 0.82 (t, J = 7.3
Hz, 1.5H), 0.79 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1.5H), 0.51-0.44 (m, 6H). 13C NMR(100MHz,
CDCl3): I 146.3, 145.3, 144.2, 144.1, 143.8, 143.7, 140.4, 140.0, 137.8,
137.6, 129.7, 129.7, 128.4, 128.3, 128.1, 127.9, 127.7, 127.6, 125.8,
125.7, 73.5, 73.4, 70.4, 70.4, 39.4, 39.3, 30.2, 29.8, 21.6, 10.5, 10.4,
6.8, 4.7, 4.7. IR (film): 3508 (br), 3085, 3062, 3029, 2956, 2911, 2876,
1640, 1598, 1493, 1454, 1412, 1378, 1287, 1239, 1196, 1183, 1145, 1084,
1017 cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3): m/z 492 (M+NH4 +), 475 (M+H+). Anal. Calcd
for C26H38O4SSi: C, 65.78; H, 8.07. Found: C, 65.66; H, 8.05.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective ((E olefin), 1:1 mixt. of diastereomers), 65% isolated
yield of product
