$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Catalytic
Cyclization and the Subsequent Reaction with Electrophiles A solution of
methallylmagnesium chloride (2.25 mL, 0.89 M solution in THF, 2.0 mmol)
was added to a solution of CrCl3 (4 mg, 0.025 mmol) in THF at 0 °C. After
stirring for 20 min, to the resulting yellow solution was added allyl
non-2-yn-1-yl ether (1a, 90 mg, 0.5 mmol) in THF and the mixture was
heated at 40 °C with stirring for 5 h. The reaction mixture was then
cooled to 0 °C. To the reaction mixture was added allyl bromide (0.19 mL,
2.25 mmol) followed by a solution of CuCN.2LiCl (0.1 mL, 1.0 M in THF,
0.1 mmol). The mixture was stirred for another 45 min. The mixture was
then poured into 1 M HCl aq. and extracted with ether (3 × 10 mL). The
organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by silica gel column chromatography (hexane/ethyl acetate =
10/1) afforded 5d (121 mg, 0.41 mmol) in 82% yield.
3-(1-Hexyl-3-methylbut-3-enylidene)-4-(2-hydroxy-2-phenylethyl)tetrahydrofuran
(5a), yield 164 mg, 84% IR (neat) 3412, 2930, 1454, 1069, 889, 700 cm-1;
1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 0.88 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.17.1.40 (m, 8H), 1.60 (s,
3H), 1.74.1.88 (m, 2H), 1.74.1.88 (m, 1H), 1.93.2.03 (m, 2H), 2.55 (d, J
= 15.6 Hz, 1H), 2.63.2.70 (m, 1H), 2.72 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 3.69 (dd, J
= 8.7, 5.1 Hz, 1H), 3.89 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 4.24 (d, J = 12.9 Hz, 1H),
4.37 (d, J = 12.9 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (s, 1H), 4.60.4.69 (m, 1H), 4.73 (s, 1H),
7.20.7.40 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 13.92, 22.35, 22.50, 27.73, 29.18,
31.64, 32.30, 39.26, 40.53, 42.65, 68.83, 73.51, 73.68, 111.25, 126.07,
127.83, 128.64, 128.97, 138.59, 143.59, 143.56, 144.55. Found: C, 80.59;
H, 10.15%. Calcd for C23H34O2: C, 80.65; H, 10.01%.
