$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Triethyl-hex-5-en-3-ynyloxy-sliane: To a
stirred solution of vinyl bromide (1.0 M solution of THF, 18 mL, 18.0
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (208 mg, 0.18 mmol), CuI (91.6 mg, 0.48 mmol), and Et3N
(3.4 mL, 24.0 mmol) was added a solution of but-3-ynyloxy-triethylsilane
(2.21 g, 12.0 mmol) in THF (6 mL) via a syringe pump over 1 hour. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 hours and then it
was filtered through Celite. The solvent was removed in vacuo.
Purification of residue by flash chromatography (SiO2: Rf = 0.72,
hexanes/EtOAc = 20/1) gave the enyne product.
2-Hydroxy-3-(4-nitro-phenyl)-hexa-3,5-dienoic acid ethyl ester, yield
75%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): 8.21 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.42 (d, J = 9.0
Hz, 2H), 6.54 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 6.19 (ddd, J = 10.8, 11.1, 17.1 Hz,
1H), 5.46 (dd, J = 17.1, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.26 (dd, J = 11.1, 1.5 Hz, 1H),
4.89 (s, 1H), 4.16 (m, 2H), 3.40 (s, 1H), 1.16 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): 172.6, 147.2, 143.6, 136.9, 133.4, 132.1, 130.4,
123.3, 122.1, 74.9, 62.4, 14.0. HRMS Calcd. for C14H16NO5 (M): 278.1028,
Found: 278.1031. FTIR (neat): 3486, 2982, 1732, 1599, 1519, 1347, 1210,
1108, 1015, 921, 856, 715 cm-1. HPLC (Chiralcel OD-H column, 4%
i-PrOH/hexanes, 0.5 mL/min, 254 nm), tmajor = 27.0 min, tminor = 28.7
min; ee = 97%.[α]D = + 48.8 (c = 3.25, CH2Cl2).
