$DATUM (2S,4R,5S,6E,8S,10S,12S)-2-Benzoyloxy-5-hydroxy-4,6,8,10,12-pentamethyl-pentadec-6-en-3-one
(8). To a solution of c-Hex2BCl (0.37 g, 0.39 mL, 1.8 mmol) in Et2O (5
mL) was added Me2NEt (0.16 g, 0.23 mL, 2.1 mmol). A solution of the
(2S)-benzoyloxy-3-pentanone (0.24 g, 1.2 mmol) in Et2O(2 mL) was added
-78 °C. The resultant suspension was stirred 10 min at -78 °C, 2 h at 0
°C, and recooled to -78 °C. A solution of freshly prepared siphonarienal
(0.22 g, 1.2 mmol) in Et2O (2 mL) was added. After 1 h at -78 °C, the
solution was placed in the freezer overnight (-20 °C). The reaction
mixture was warmed to 0 °C and quenched with a mixture of MeOH (2 mL) and
pH 7 buffer (4 mL) followed by 30% aq H2O2 (2 mL). After 1 h at 0 °C, the
layers were separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O. The
combined organic extracts were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by column chromatography (5% to 8%
EtOAc/hexane) to afford the title compound (0.35 g, 82% yield). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 0.7-1.0 (m, 16 H), 1.0-1.5 (m, 9 H), 1.55 (d, J=7.1 Hz, 3 H),
1.59 (s, 3 H), 1.85-2.05 (bs, 1 H), 2.4-2.6 (m, 1 H), 2.95-3.1 (m, 1 H),
4.16 (d, J=9.5 Hz, 1 H), 5.10 (d, J=9.5 Hz, 1 H), 5.43 (q, J=7 Hz, 1 H),
7.42 (t, J=7.3 Hz, 2 H), 7.55 (t, J=7.3 Hz, 1 H), 8.05 (d, J=8.0 Hz, 2
H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 10.35, 14.36, 14.42, 15.51, 19.95, 20.02, 20.04,
21.63, 28.09, 29.54, 29.65, 39.21, 44.80, 45.28, 45.81, 75.14, 80.58,
128.36 (2C), 129.59, 129.75 (2C), 132.56, 133.18, 136.92, 165.83, 210.95.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
