$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Compounds 9-19 and 25. To a stirred solution of appropriate aldehyde
(1.00 mmol) in CH3 CN (2.7 mL), activated olefin (3.00 mmol) and water
(0.3 mL) were added. DABCO (112 mg, 1.00 mmol) was then added to the
mixture, and the reaction was allowed to stir at room temperature for 7
days. The mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 (25 mL) and washed with 1 N HCl
(3 × 25 mL) and brine (30 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and the solvent evaporated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by FC as indicated.
Ethyl 2-((2-Fluorophenyl)(hydroxy)methyl)acrylate (10). The product was
obtained using 2-fluorobenzaldehyde and ethyl acrylate. The crude product
was purified by FC eluting with PE/EtOAc 9/1 to afford 10 as a yellowish
oil (0.709 mmol, 159.2 mg, 71% yield). MS/CI (isobutane): [M-H]+ 225; 1H
NMR (CDCl3): δ, 7.43-7.11 (m, 2H, ArH), 7.05-6.94 (m, 2H, ArH), 6.34 (s,
1H, C═CH), 5.88 (s, 1H, CH), 5.81 (s, 1H, C═CH), 4.17 (q, 2H, J = 7.2 Hz,
OCH2), 3.91 (s, 1H, OH), 0.85 (t, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz, CH3); 13C NMR (CDCl3):
δ, 166.1, 159.8, 141.0, 129.0, 128.5, 128.0, 125.6, 124.0, 115.3, 66.6,
60.9, 13.6. cLogP: 1.97. TC50: 25.4 ± 2.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, Morita-Baylis-Hillman reaction
