$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To 7 (0.12 g, 0.576 mmol) in 5ml THF at room temperature was added BuLi
(2.5M in hexane, 0.253 ml, 0.634 mmol) and the resulting was refluxed
under nitrogen for 2h, cooled to –78°C and freshly distilled acrolein
(64.6 mg, 1.152 mmol) added to it. The resulting was stirred at room
temperature for 2h, quenched with water and saturated ammonium chloride
solution. The aqueous layer was extracted with ether (2x10ml). Organic
layer was dried over MgSO4, concentrated and chromatographed (5-10% ethyl
acetate in petroleum ether) 1-(2,6-Dimethoxy-4-pentyl phenyl)
prop-2-en-1-ol, 10, yield 91% Rf = 0.41 (10% ethyl acetate in petroleum
ether). IR (thin film): 3560.6, 2932.7, 2857.9, 1610.0, 1583.1, 1457.5,
1420.4, 1233.9, 1121.7 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 6.385 (s, 2H),
6.162 (ddd, J = 17.09, 10.254, 5.37 Hz, 1H), 5.61 (OH, 1H), 5-5.22 (m,
2H), 3.929 (d, J = 11.475 Hz, 1H), 3.82 (s, 6H), 2.559 (t, J = 7.813 Hz,
2H), 1.5-1.7 (m, 2H), 1.25-1.4 (m, 4H), 0.9 (t, J = 6.837 Hz, 3H). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 157.42, 144.13, 140.43, 115.66, 113.05, 104.6,
55.72, 36.53, 31.52, 31.06, 22.52, 14.02. Elemental analysis calculated
for C16H24O3 C, 72.69; H, 9.15; found: C, 72.71; H, 8.92.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM last stage quench
