$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 60-29-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Allylmagnesium chloride (1.0 M in Et2O, 1.2
equiv) was added dropwise to a stirred solution of the aldehyde (1 equiv)
dissolved in dry Et2O (3 mL/mol) at 0°C. The resulting suspension was
stirred at room temperature overnight and then quenched by addition of
saturated ammonium chloride, extracted with EtOAc (×3). The combined
organic layer was washed with saturated brine (×1), dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and evaporated. The crude products were purified by flash
chromatography. 1-(2,3,4-trimethoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (2d). Product 2d
was isolated by flash chromatography (PE:EA = 10:1) in 88% yield as light
yellow liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.03 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 6.66
(d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 5.90-5.79 (m, 1H), 5.17-5.09 (m, 2H), 4.90 (dd, J =
7.6, 5.5 Hz, 2H), 3.93 (s, 3H), 3.86 (s, 3H), 3.85 (s, 3H), 2.59-2.43 (m,
3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.0, 150.9, 141.8, 135.0, 129.4, 121.0,
117.7, 107.1, 69.0, 61.1, 60.6, 55.9, 42.7; IR (KBr) 3522, 3360, 3075,
2938, 2837, 1640, 1600, 1495, 1464, 1418, 1277, 1231, 1199, 1165, 1095,
1016, 914, 872, 849, 804, 691, 667, 526; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
